# Paper 1 — Frame Constraints and the Limits of Totalization

**Status:** Acted  
**Repository:** Geoffrey.Marcellin  
**DOI:** 10.5281/zenodo.18199983  

## Abstract
This paper introduces a minimal operational framework for systems operating under finite informational access, energetic cost, and constrained feedback.  
It establishes a set of structural invariants showing why total observation, control, and prediction are jointly unattainable under finite resources.

## Scope
- Framework-level invariant
- No new physical postulates
- Compatible with existing mathematics and physics

## Notes
This paper serves as the foundational reference for all subsequent developments.
